{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry","id":545030,"title":"[2.5e Solar Melee Charm] - Dual Wielding Parry?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-08T05:13:51-07:00","id":545030,"title":"[2.5e Solar Melee Charm] - Dual Wielding Parry?","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> I've been getting back into the Exalted mood after a long hiatus, and had an idea for a charm that I wanted some opinions on. The concept is a Permanent Charm that alleviates penalties for dual-wielding non-paired weapons, and in addition allows the Solar to reflexively spend a small amount of motes to apply the defense statistic of both weapons to her DV (think both weapons simultaneously blocking an attack) in Step 2 of the attack resolution. For the active portion, I was thinking of somewhere along the lines of 1m for an instant duration, 3m for a tick-long benefit, and 3m 1wp for a scene-long benefit (available at higher essence).<br /> <br /> I'm unsure right now of suitable prerequisite charms (my gut says One Weapon Two Blows, or none at all), fitting Minimum stat requirements (Melee 4 Essence 2? Essence 3 for the scene-long benefit?), and how to tweak the costs.<br /> <br /> Feel free to give your honest comments and criticism, I can take it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:08:10-07:00","id":545101,"title":"","content":"Way too cheap for the active effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T07:39:39-07:00","id":545158,"title":"","content":"What are the high end of 2e parry bonuses? +6 or +7? Yeah, 1m for +3 or +4 DV sounds too cheap. Of course, 3m is practically the 3rd Excellency, so maybe 3m is about right?<br /> <br /> Is this subject to dice-adder caps? It's kinda sorta not really a dice adder, since it's doing it through more equipment bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:37:47-07:00","id":545343,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd put it at ~4 for instant, 5 for tick and something like 7 for scene. I(A)M is going to boost PDV by, what, 5 for the scene for 20 motes (on top of all attacks etc)? Sounds about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T09:18:05-07:00","id":545387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=545158#post545158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the high end of 2e parry bonuses? +6 or +7? Yeah, 1m for +3 or +4 DV sounds too cheap. Of course, 3m is practically the 3rd Excellency, so maybe 3m is about right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind Hand Manipulation:<br /> Willpower 10 + Occult 5 + Telekinesis specialty 3 + Force Suppression Barrier (Essence)<br /> <br /> Minimum PDV = 10<br /> Max at E5 = 12","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:31:44-07:00","id":545878,"title":"","content":"Note that the above costs 14m, and is then available repeatedly for one scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 06-08-2015, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:44:19-07:00","id":547564,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the responses! I thought cost might be an issue, thanks for the clarifications on that. Do you think the scenelong activation should have a willpower cost, or just a mote cost?<br /> <br /> Also, how do the minima look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T17:56:13-07:00","id":547801,"title":"","content":"Scene longs generally cost willpower yeah.<br /> <br /> Requirements looked great. E2 for instant, E3 for scene-long.4m for instant, and what should scene-long be set at? 10m1w?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:14:18-07:00","id":548148,"title":"","content":"No idea. I'm wondering if it should even have a scene-long, since I forgot how much the concept of breaking dice adder caps means in terms of Solar power. My gut says 3m for the active (E2 minima), 5m for a tick (E2 minima), and 8m1wp for a possible scenelong (E3 minima) - but that latter part may be removed.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:07:19-07:00","id":548427,"title":"","content":"The scene long effectively stacks an equipment bonus with the already formidable I(A)M. Which potentially works out to base PDV + 5 + (2nd weapon's Defense / 2). Assuming optimized for defense weapons and that latter value could be something like +6/+7 before being halved, which translates to PDV +8, where it's already easy to be sitting at PDV 10 just from Dex 5/Melee 5/Specialty 3/Defense +6/+7. For a grand total of PDV 18. <br /> <br /> Yeah I don't think that's a good thing to be longer than a tick or an action AT BEST and the action long should be costly. <br /> <br /> Of course it bears the question - if it's so expensive for such a short term benefit, why not just throw out a much cheaper instant HGD + flurry breaker?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:11:47-07:00","id":548468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=548427#post548427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scene long effectively stacks an equipment bonus with the already formidable I(A)M. Which potentially works out to base PDV + 5 + (2nd weapon's Defense / 2). Assuming optimized for defense weapons and that latter value could be something like +6/+7 before being halved, which translates to PDV +8, where it's already easy to be sitting at PDV 10 just from Dex 5/Melee 5/Specialty 3/Defense +6/+7. For a grand total of PDV 18. <br /> <br /> Yeah I don't think that's a good thing to be longer than a tick or an action AT BEST and the action long should be costly. <br /> <br /> Of course it bears the question - if it's so expensive for such a short term benefit, why not just throw out a much cheaper instant HGD + flurry breaker?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does jumping your PDV up by +4 for a tick qualify as a flurry breaker? That does mean stuff to the accuracy bell curve. Should lower chance to hit from something like 50% to 5% right?<br /> <br /> If that's the case, make it a 4m tick-long Charm?<br /> <br /> Edit: Huh. Couldn't find my usual Exalted probability table to come back with real numbers. Poop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":4729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","user":"Childofthesun1","date":". 06-10-2015, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T18:21:31-07:00","id":549562,"title":"","content":"No a flurry breaker would allow you to move out of range or no longer be a valid target for a melee flurry, as LDM does in Dodge. Still standing there and having insane PDV doesn't render you immune to the flurry and you still take DV degradation from onslaught, etc unless you invest more motes into other charms. A hit could get through especially versus opponents also throwing Excellencies + accurate Artifact weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T07:04:57-07:00","id":550075,"title":"","content":"Sorry I meant something more along the lines of &quot;could ramping your DV to insane levels serve the same purpose as a flurry breaker? Could that be the purpose of this Charm?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd be interested to see a version of the Charm that adds the offhand defense value and cancels all penalties due to onslaught or coordinated attacks for one tick, for maybe 6/7m. That'd be a neat answer to flurries for melee, since melee has no flurry breakers (I think?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:50:53-07:00","id":550758,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really serve the same purpose. A flurry breaker makes you not an applicable target by getting out of attack range. This Charm just greatly decreases your chance of being hit, but you're still a valid target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:07:59-07:00","id":550878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=550758#post550758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't really serve the same purpose. A flurry breaker makes you not an applicable target by getting out of attack range. This Charm just greatly decreases your chance of being hit, but you're still a valid target.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Unhittable&quot; and &quot;nigh-unhittable&quot; are nearly identical states of being. I think that would be an interesting design space for this Charm, if that can be made to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:24:26-07:00","id":551025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=550075#post550075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I meant something more along the lines of &quot;could ramping your DV to insane levels serve the same purpose as a flurry breaker? Could that be the purpose of this Charm?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd be interested to see a version of the Charm that adds the offhand defense value and cancels all penalties due to onslaught or coordinated attacks for one tick, for maybe 6/7m. That'd be a neat answer to flurries for melee, since melee has no flurry breakers (I think?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just Bulwark stance plus the second excellency? With perhaps a tad of a discount if you have a really high defense weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T21:16:39-07:00","id":551064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=551025#post551025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that just Bulwark stance plus the second excellency? With perhaps a tad of a discount if you have a really high defense weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div> That stacks with I(A)M because it's an equipment bonus. So at E2 yes. At E 3 or 4, it's more than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T23:10:19-07:00","id":551149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=551025#post551025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that just Bulwark stance plus the second excellency? With perhaps a tad of a discount if you have a really high defense weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think this Charm needs to cancel penalties at all - Dipping Swallow Defense and its branches manage that just fine. My intention for this Charm was to simply provide a means of using both weapons in defense, rather than one. It's supposed to provide options for fighting with two weapons beyond &quot;Defense Sword and Attack Sword.&quot; Sidestepping die adder caps is powerful, yes, so the cost should fit that. I could potentially make it do otherwise, but then it's no different than an excellency that removes a -1 internal penalty for offhanded actions, which is boring.<br /> <br /> Cost-wise, I'm thinking 3m for instant, mostly because from what I've seen of the Errata'd non-shield artifact weapons defense bonuses cap somewhere around +4-5 after Charm benefits such as Sun-Sword Concentration (which basically results in a doubling of the Ori MM bonuses). I've decided the scene-length benefit is just too much, so I thought up a potential alternate approach after reading MoEP: Infernals again. I'm considering borrowing the cost reduction benefit from Pathetic Distraction Rebuke (PDR) as follows:<br /> <br /> At Essence 3, repeated uses of this Charm reduce its cost cumulatively by one mote each iteration, to a minimum of 0m, until the Solar's next action. A second activation of Sun and Moon Stance (working name) during the same action will cost 2m, and a third 1m, and so on.<br /> <br /> Effectively, this fixes the tick-length and action-length costs as equivalent. I'm considering making the E3 benefit like PDR, with which it requires a 2nd purchase.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T04:01:30-07:00","id":551236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=550878#post550878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Unhittable&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;nigh-unhittable&amp;quot; are nearly identical states of being. I think that would be an interesting design space for this Charm, if that can be made to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're distinctly different in terms of Charm technology. <br /> <br /> &quot;Cannot target&quot; is mechanically distinct from &quot;targetable but practically unhittable.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=551149#post551149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sun and Moon Stance (working name)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know my knee jerk reaction reading the first post was &quot;huh sounds like some attempt at porting the 1e Steel Devil Style cascade.&quot; I see I was right. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T04:38:11-07:00","id":551262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=551149#post551149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I don't think this Charm needs to cancel penalties at all - Dipping Swallow Defense and its branches manage that just fine. My intention for this Charm was to simply provide a means of using both weapons in defense, rather than one. It's supposed to provide options for fighting with two weapons beyond &amp;quot;Defense Sword and Attack Sword.&amp;quot; Sidestepping die adder caps is powerful, yes, so the cost should fit that. I could potentially make it do otherwise, but then it's no different than an excellency that removes a -1 internal penalty for offhanded actions, which is boring.<br /> <br /> Cost-wise, I'm thinking 3m for instant, mostly because from what I've seen of the Errata'd non-shield artifact weapons defense bonuses cap somewhere around +4-5 after Charm benefits such as Sun-Sword Concentration (which basically results in a doubling of the Ori MM bonuses). I've decided the scene-length benefit is just too much, so I thought up a potential alternate approach after reading MoEP: Infernals again. I'm considering borrowing the cost reduction benefit from Pathetic Distraction Rebuke (PDR) as follows:<br /> <br /> At Essence 3, repeated uses of this Charm reduce its cost cumulatively by one mote each iteration, to a minimum of 0m, until the Solar's next action. A second activation of Sun and Moon Stance (working name) during the same action will cost 2m, and a third 1m, and so on.<br /> <br /> Effectively, this fixes the tick-length and action-length costs as equivalent. I'm considering making the E3 benefit like PDR, with which it requires a 2nd purchase.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was just an idea. Looks great!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=551236#post551236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're distinctly different in terms of Charm technology. <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Cannot target&amp;quot; is mechanically distinct from &amp;quot;targetable but practically unhittable.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> You know my knee jerk reaction reading the first post was &amp;quot;huh sounds like some attempt at porting the 1e Steel Devil Style cascade.&amp;quot; I see I was right. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in the strictest of senses. As long as your opponent is not overwhelmingly more powerful, the end effect is the same. The flurry misses. Though whether +7 defense creates a situation of being practically unhittable is up for debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:25:24-07:00","id":551555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=551236#post551236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know my knee jerk reaction reading the first post was &quot;huh sounds like some attempt at porting the 1e Steel Devil Style cascade.&quot; I see I was right. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, you caught me. But to be entirely honest, I only lifted the name - I swear! The Charms themselves didn't really provide much in the way of inspiration because of how different 1e and 2e are when it comes to combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It was just an idea. Looks great!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! And no prob, I hope I didn't come off as too dismissive there. I feel pretty safe with the essence of the Charm (dual weapon parry), I just want to make sure that the numbers and extra bits look kosher. Do you think the E3 effect warrants a second purchase, or is it fine just automatically coming into being?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:42:25-07:00","id":551581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=551262#post551262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only in the strictest of senses. As long as your opponent is not overwhelmingly more powerful, the end effect is the same. The flurry misses. Though whether +7 defense creates a situation of being practically unhittable is up for debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't - remember that perfect attacks are a thing. Also remember that you can't use a perfect attack against something that isn't a valid target.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:01:28-07:00","id":551748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/545030-2-5e-solar-melee-charm-dual-wielding-parry?p=551581#post551581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't - remember that perfect attacks are a thing. Also remember that you can't use a perfect attack against something that isn't a valid target.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one situation where the distinction matters. And I have never seen a flurry of perfect attacks, every one of which requires willpower to the best of my knowledge. It is a good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}